/E (Because every instruction is given exactly 4 consecutive ROM words \(states T0 through T3\), the address naturally decomposes as address = opcode\(4 bits\) x 4 + step\(2 bits\). This is exactly why the ROM is 64 words and not 16 or 32 words: 16 possible opcodes x 4 microsteps = 64, with no wasted space and no padding.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
