/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 131 0 R
/T (Initialize: A = 0,Q = multiplier, Q-1 = 0, M = multiplicand, counter= 13.)
/E (Initialize: A = 0,Q = multiplier, Q-1 = 0, M = multiplicand, counter= 13.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [28]
>>
endobj
653 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 131 0 R
/T (Each of 13 iterations: examine \(Q0, Q-1\). If 01, do A <- A + M. If 10, do A <- A - M. If 00 or 11, do nothing. Arithmetic-right-shift the combined A:Q:Q-1 register one place \(sign-extending A's top bit\), which simultaneously  shifts A's new LSB into Q's MSB and Q's old LSB into Q-1. Decrement the counter; repeat until it reaches zero. After 13 iterations, the signed 26-bit product is the concatenation A:Q.)
/E (Each of 13 iterations: examine \(Q0, Q-1\). If 01, do A <- A + M. If 10, do A <- A - M. If 00 or 11, do nothing. Arithmetic-right-shift the combined A:Q:Q-1 register one place \(sign-extending A's top bit\), which simultaneously  shifts A's new LSB into Q's MSB and Q's old LSB into Q-1. Decrement the counter; repeat until it reaches zero. After 13 iterations, the signed 26-bit product is the concatenation A:Q.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [29]
>>
endobj
